P-BUILD-001 (branding slice 1) — UA product token and client-hints brand "ReArc".

Warm-up for the overlay pipeline: the smallest real divergence from stock
Chromium. Two mechanical hunks:
1. components/version_info/version_info_with_user_agent.cc — the User-Agent
   product token becomes "ReArc/<version>" (was "Chrome/<version>"), full and
   reduced UA forms.
2. components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc — the base-project brand in
   the Sec-CH-UA brand list becomes "ReArc" (was "Chromium").
No behavior change beyond advertised tokens. NOTE: both touched files live in
components/, so patches/README.md area rules would place this under
components/; it is kept at the task-specified chrome/ path.

Drift note (2026-11-01): components/version_info/version_info.cc no longer
exists at this pin; product naming moved to generated
base/version_info/version_info_values.h (PRODUCT_NAME), which rule 6 forbids
patching. The UA token functions above are the compilable branding surface.

Last rebased: 2026-11-01 @ Chromium 156.0.8078.74
(d331de35ca8ab1358c7a17e4bd41627d55eaef51).

